            <ArticleTitle>Truly unentangled photon pairs without spectral filtering.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3638-3641</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1364/OL.42.003638</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We demonstrate that an integrated silicon microring resonator is capable of efficiently producing photon pairs that are completely unentangled; such pairs are a key component of heralded single-photon sources. A dual-channel interferometric coupling scheme can be used to independently tune the quality factors associated with the pump and signal and idler modes, yielding a biphoton wavefunction with a Schmidt number arbitrarily close to unity. This will permit the generation of heralded single-photon states with unit purity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
